WEBVTT

1

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.625

Let's move!



2

00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:40.417

Hange?



3

00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:43.000

G-Get me a horse.



4

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.208

Section Commander! Where are you trying to go?



5

00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:50.000

To that village where we captured

the Titan who couldn't walk.



6

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.500

You mean Ragako?



7

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.958

I need to see it... with my own eyes.



8

00:00:53.958 --> 00:00:56.167

Don't say something so ridiculous!



9

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:59.667

Your body can't take riding a horse right now!



10

00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:05.542

I have a hunch... that we need to investigate...



11

00:01:08.292 --> 00:01:09.708

All right.



12

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:15.250

I'll go there on my own,

so you just stay here and faint or something.



13

00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:24.750

Spread out! Take formation to locate any enemies!



14

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:36.042

Eren...



15

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.000

"Opening"



16

00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:17.958

Oh, Eren?



17

00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:19.583

You're awake?



18

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:40.542

What the hell?!



19

00:03:40.542 --> 00:03:42.833

My arms!



20

00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:44.375

Eren.



21

00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:47.875

Look at me. I'm in the same shape as you.



22

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:50.625

Guess the both of us are having a bad day.



23

00:03:50.625 --> 00:03:52.667

Ymir...



24

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:55.625

Why... don't I have any arms?



25

00:03:55.625 --> 00:03:57.250

That's my bad.



26

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.250

I'm the one who did that.



27

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:03.458

I kinda was in a hurry.



28

00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:09.083

When I rushed to bite your nape,

I neglected to take your arms into account.



29

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.708

I see...



30

00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:17.167

I... must've lost.



31

00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:28.708

Eren, stop!



32

00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:31.125

Hold your horses, Eren.



33

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:33.625

Take a good look around us.



34

00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:37.167

We're in the giant forest within Wall Maria.



35

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:40.750

It's not even close to any of the walls.



36

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.667

In other words, we're deep in Titan territory.



37

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.500

Take a look.



38

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.000

I think that one down there's an Abnormal.



39

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.917

It looks like he's just lounging around,

but he's not taking his eyes off us.



40

00:04:55.917 --> 00:04:58.083

There's a lot of small ones down there, too.



41

00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:00.458

That alone is dangerous.



42

00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:03.375

Over that way's another big one.



43

00:05:03.375 --> 00:05:06.292

He staring at us, but won't come any closer.



44

00:05:06.292 --> 00:05:09.917

I bet you that one's a scaredy-cat.



45

00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:12.333

And then you've got these chumps.



46

00:05:12.333 --> 00:05:14.208

Those dirty bastards.



47

00:05:14.208 --> 00:05:17.750

They're the only ones with any ODM gear on.



48

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.625

Reiner's wearing gear he took from you.



49

00:05:20.625 --> 00:05:25.083

So I don't think changing into a Titan

at this point is going to solve anything.



50

00:05:25.083 --> 00:05:30.458

Not only can they do that, but they can

escape high into the trees as well.



51

00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:33.917

Those two aside, there's Titans all around us.



52

00:05:33.917 --> 00:05:39.625

Escaping out of this Titan territory

would be tough, even with Titan powers.



53

00:05:40.625 --> 00:05:42.208

Understand?



54

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.375

There's nothing to gain by acting up.



55

00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:47.125

No.



56

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:49.917

You two can't even turn into Titans right now.



57

00:05:49.917 --> 00:05:53.458

So don't count on that to help you.



58

00:05:53.458 --> 00:05:55.417

Your body is at its limit.



59

00:05:55.417 --> 00:05:59.500

It's taking everything you've got

to repair the damage.



60

00:06:00.875 --> 00:06:02.167

Are you stupid?



61

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.750

Why the hell would I trust anything

coming out of your mouth?



62

00:06:09.458 --> 00:06:10.542

Well...



63

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:15.708

It's not like I know the specifics

behind how Titan powers work.



64

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:20.125

Unlike you guys, I'm pretty clueless about it.



65

00:06:20.125 --> 00:06:22.375

Hey, Reiner.



66

00:06:22.375 --> 00:06:25.875

You said you would talk once Eren woke up.



67

00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:30.083

It's about time one of you says

what you plan to do with us.



68

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:35.458

We'll take you to our hometown.



69

00:06:35.458 --> 00:06:39.708

I realize that you're not

going to listen and do as I say.



70

00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:44.042

But like Ymir was saying,

this place is swarming with Titans.



71

00:06:44.042 --> 00:06:46.708

We could beat the shit out of each other right now,



72

00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:50.750

but when we're weak, the other Titans

would just come and eat us.



73

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:56.750

So until nightfall, when the Titans can't move,

we have no choice but to wait here.



74

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.583

Whether you try to run and escape from us...



75

00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:02.875

...or don't and we take you away...



76

00:07:02.875 --> 00:07:06.125

...either way, we wait for night.



77

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:09.708

Why didn't you stay

the Armored Titan and run home?



78

00:07:09.708 --> 00:07:12.583

What's the point of stopping here?



79

00:07:12.583 --> 00:07:15.750

Too tired and had to take a break?



80

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:18.625

Why don't you use your imagination?



81

00:07:22.083 --> 00:07:24.042

Let's think...



82

00:07:24.042 --> 00:07:26.708

If I waited for an opening and became a Titan,



83

00:07:26.708 --> 00:07:31.875

running away from here doesn't seem

like it would pose a challenge.



84

00:07:31.875 --> 00:07:36.458

But will I be able to transform

into a Titan in the first place?



85

00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:40.167

Reiner said that I can't...



86

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:45.292

And I have to consider that even Reiner

had to stop here to take a break.



87

00:07:45.292 --> 00:07:51.208

If my Titan form isn't strong enough,

does that mean I'll just get eaten by the others?



88

00:07:53.833 --> 00:07:56.875

Are you simply waiting here for it to become night?



89

00:07:56.875 --> 00:07:58.833

Maybe I am.



90

00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:02.667

No... There's no way they'd wait until nightfall.



91

00:08:02.667 --> 00:08:07.417

They're not going to give our bodies

the chance to fully recover.



92

00:08:07.417 --> 00:08:10.875

They'll make their move

while we're still powerless.



93

00:08:12.583 --> 00:08:15.042

At this rate, I can't do anything.



94

00:08:15.042 --> 00:08:16.875

At this rate...



95

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.208

What happened to everybody?



96

00:08:22.208 --> 00:08:23.958

Where are the Scouts?



97

00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:30.333

Don't tell me they're coming this way...



98

00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:33.292

If they try to help,

no one's gonna make it back safely.



99

00:08:33.292 --> 00:08:38.125

What's it matter? Those Titans at the castle

moved just fine at night.



100

00:08:38.125 --> 00:08:40.250

Won't these Titans, too?



101

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:43.083

The Titans here can't move at night.



102

00:08:43.083 --> 00:08:46.917

You should know all about it, Ymir.



103

00:08:49.583 --> 00:08:53.250

Speaking of which,

why can Ymir turn into a Titan?



104

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:57.125

I don't think she's like me,

who knew nothing about it.



105

00:08:57.125 --> 00:08:59.125

Is she on our side?



106

00:08:59.125 --> 00:09:01.917

I don't even know what her goal is yet.



107

00:09:01.917 --> 00:09:05.125

She's hard enough to understand as it is.



108

00:09:07.167 --> 00:09:09.208

I've made up my mind.



109

00:09:09.208 --> 00:09:13.167

Right now, what I need is information.



110

00:09:13.167 --> 00:09:16.792

I need to figure out

everything I can from these guys.



111

00:09:16.792 --> 00:09:20.333

And then I'll make my escape.



112

00:09:20.333 --> 00:09:22.625

To do that, I need...



113

00:09:24.292 --> 00:09:27.375

...to suppress all my emotions...



114

00:09:27.375 --> 00:09:30.000

...and for my body to heal.



115

00:09:30.917 --> 00:09:35.917

"Those with the power to become Titans

possess an inherent ability to regenerate."



116

00:09:40.208 --> 00:09:44.208

Titan spotted at three 'o clock! Fire the smoke!



117

00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:46.875

Smoke shell confirmed on the right wing!



118

00:09:46.875 --> 00:09:48.333

Do not change direction!



119

00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:51.833

Have the right wing merge

with the center and hold course!



120

00:09:51.833 --> 00:09:53.958

We only have until sunset!



121

00:09:53.958 --> 00:09:57.083

We must take the shortest possible path!



122

00:09:59.583 --> 00:10:01.333

Mikasa.



123

00:10:01.333 --> 00:10:03.042

Hey, Mikasa!



124

00:10:03.042 --> 00:10:05.167

Mikasa!



125

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:07.083

Stop pushing so hard.



126

00:10:07.083 --> 00:10:09.333

You're drifting near the vanguard.



127

00:10:09.333 --> 00:10:12.167

It'll ruin the whole formation.



128

00:10:12.167 --> 00:10:15.250

I know how you feel, but... didn't I tell you?



129

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:19.208

Eren won't get taken away

without putting up a fight.



130

00:10:19.208 --> 00:10:20.667

Don't you agree?



131

00:10:22.708 --> 00:10:25.042

You know he'll never give up.



132

00:10:25.042 --> 00:10:29.750

So it's up to us to stay calm

and be there when he needs us.



133

00:10:33.292 --> 00:10:35.583

Just like we did back then.



134

00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:00.000

Reiner.



135

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.833

You got any water?



136

00:11:01.833 --> 00:11:05.417

If I don't get some soon,

I'm going to dry up and die.



137

00:11:05.417 --> 00:11:11.625

Even if it's a matter of life and death,

there's nothing we can do given our situation.



138

00:11:11.625 --> 00:11:16.958

He's completely right...

This situation couldn't be any shittier.



139

00:11:18.833 --> 00:11:20.542

Speaking of which...



140

00:11:20.542 --> 00:11:26.500

Ever since the Titans showed up yesterday morning,

we've been working our asses off.



141

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:30.500

With nothing to eat or drink

and not even a wink of sleep.



142

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:34.583

Fortunately, the wall wasn't broken or anything.



143

00:11:34.583 --> 00:11:37.667

So I think we deserve to take a break for once.



144

00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:41.417

We'll see about getting promoted later.



145

00:11:41.417 --> 00:11:42.917

Reiner...



146

00:11:44.083 --> 00:11:48.875

What? We've done plenty enough to deserve it.



147

00:11:48.875 --> 00:11:53.792

I think we've performed outstandingly,

considering all we've been put through.



148

00:11:53.792 --> 00:11:58.042

I know soldiers like us are expected

to fulfill their duties, but...



149

00:11:58.042 --> 00:12:00.667

I think we've all earned it.



150

00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:09.042

Reiner...



151

00:12:09.042 --> 00:12:11.708

What in the world are you talking about?



152

00:12:11.708 --> 00:12:13.708

Huh? What do you mean?



153

00:12:13.708 --> 00:12:17.375

I'm not saying we go demand to be

promoted to captains or anything.



154

00:12:17.375 --> 00:12:20.000

That's... not what I mean.



155

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:24.333

Oh, yeah. Where did you all get that cannon from?



156

00:12:24.333 --> 00:12:27.417

That really saved my ass.



157

00:12:28.625 --> 00:12:31.708

It's a good thing Christa helped me after that.



158

00:12:31.708 --> 00:12:34.625

To be honest, I think she has a thing for me.



159

00:12:34.625 --> 00:12:35.667

Hey...



160

00:12:35.667 --> 00:12:38.875

Now that I think about it,

Christa has always treated me especially--



161

00:12:38.875 --> 00:12:40.125

Hey!



162

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:47.917

You bastard... You've gotta be kidding me.



163

00:12:49.917 --> 00:12:51.208

Huh?



164

00:12:51.208 --> 00:12:53.333

What are you so angry about, Eren?



165

00:12:53.333 --> 00:12:56.042

Did I... say something wrong?



166

00:12:56.042 --> 00:12:59.167

If you want to die, just keep talking!



167

00:12:59.167 --> 00:13:01.083

Hold up, Eren.



168

00:13:01.083 --> 00:13:03.958

This isn't normal, no matter how you look at it.



169

00:13:03.958 --> 00:13:06.500

Isn't that right, Bertholdt?



170

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:12.625

If you know something,

quit with the silence and come out and say it.



171

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:13.792

Huh?



172

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.000

Reiner...



173

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.208

You're not... a soldier, remember?



174

00:13:23.208 --> 00:13:25.083

You and I...



175

00:13:25.083 --> 00:13:27.125

...we're warriors.



176

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.750

Reiner!



177

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.333

What are you doing?!



178

00:13:45.542 --> 00:13:47.208

Hey...



179

00:13:47.208 --> 00:13:48.542

Why...



180

00:13:51.167 --> 00:13:53.708

...is Marco...



181

00:13:53.708 --> 00:13:55.583

...getting eaten?



182

00:14:03.583 --> 00:14:05.167

Right.



183

00:14:05.167 --> 00:14:08.375

That's... how it is.



184

00:14:13.833 --> 00:14:15.583

Huh?



185

00:14:17.208 --> 00:14:19.208

What's he doing?



186

00:14:20.333 --> 00:14:24.708

More or less, I think I've figured it out.



187

00:14:24.708 --> 00:14:26.750

I thought it was strange.



188

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:31.583

Why would the guy who broke the wall

risk his life to save Conny?



189

00:14:31.583 --> 00:14:36.042

Everything he does is contradictory,

but he doesn't realize it himself.



190

00:14:36.042 --> 00:14:40.625

I don't know why he

ended up like this, but probably...



191

00:14:40.625 --> 00:14:44.542

He was originally a warrior

whose goal was to break the wall, but...



192

00:14:44.542 --> 00:14:47.250

...after pretending to be a soldier for so long,



193

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:51.542

he lost sight of who he was

and couldn't tell which one was real.



194

00:14:51.542 --> 00:14:52.917

No...



195

00:14:52.917 --> 00:14:58.125

Unable to bear the weight of his sins, he convinced

himself he was a soldier protecting the wall



196

00:14:58.125 --> 00:15:02.333

to maintain emotional balance

within his own heart.



197

00:15:02.333 --> 00:15:05.625

And in the end, he believed it.



198

00:15:05.625 --> 00:15:10.083

As a result, his heart was split

and his memories broken.



199

00:15:10.083 --> 00:15:14.208

This must not be the first time

Reiner's talked and made no sense...



200

00:15:14.208 --> 00:15:17.250

...judging by Bertholdt's grim expression.



201

00:15:18.417 --> 00:15:20.167

It's amazing, really.



202

00:15:20.167 --> 00:15:22.583

For someone excessively honest like you to--



203

00:15:22.583 --> 00:15:23.875

Enough!



204

00:15:25.208 --> 00:15:27.375

Shut your mouth.



205

00:15:30.667 --> 00:15:32.250

Sorry about that.



206

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.375

I might've pried too much.



207

00:15:38.208 --> 00:15:40.750

You've gotta be kidding me.



208

00:15:41.792 --> 00:15:44.875

Why are you pretending to be the victim here?



209

00:15:44.875 --> 00:15:47.917

What's your deal?



210

00:15:47.917 --> 00:15:53.125

That day, what the hell were

you thinking when you talked to us?



211

00:15:54.333 --> 00:15:56.708

Tell me, Bertholdt.



212

00:15:56.708 --> 00:16:00.000

I'm talking to you, you damn lackey.



213

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.167

I told you everything...

while you looked at me right in the eyes.



214

00:16:04.167 --> 00:16:07.167

About the day my mother was eaten alive...



215

00:16:07.167 --> 00:16:10.833

Stop!



216

00:16:10.833 --> 00:16:12.542

Isn't that right?



217

00:16:12.542 --> 00:16:16.750

Thanks to the piece of wall you kicked

that went flying straight into my house,



218

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.333

my mother couldn't escape or run away.



219

00:16:20.333 --> 00:16:24.208

You remember, right? I told you my story.



220

00:16:25.208 --> 00:16:27.833

What were you thinking?



221

00:16:27.833 --> 00:16:31.000

What were you thinking when I told you?



222

00:16:35.208 --> 00:16:37.125

Back then...



223

00:16:38.792 --> 00:16:42.500

...I thought... I felt sorry for you.



224

00:16:47.125 --> 00:16:48.750

Oh...



225

00:16:49.792 --> 00:16:52.625

I see...



226

00:16:52.625 --> 00:16:54.792

You guys...



227

00:16:54.792 --> 00:16:56.333

You guys...



228

00:16:56.333 --> 00:16:59.917

...are neither soldiers nor warriors.



229

00:16:59.917 --> 00:17:02.583

You're just murderers.



230

00:17:02.583 --> 00:17:03.917

You're psychotic mass-murderers



231

00:17:03.917 --> 00:17:07.625

who've killed countless innocent people

who never did anything wrong!



232

00:17:07.625 --> 00:17:09.583

You don't think I know that?!



233

00:17:09.583 --> 00:17:11.958

I don't need you to point that out to me!



234

00:17:11.958 --> 00:17:15.583

Then don't pretend to have emotions

like you're one of us!



235

00:17:15.583 --> 00:17:18.000

You guys aren't even human anymore!



236

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:21.250

It's you two who've turned

this world into a living hell!



237

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.792

Does that make you happy, murderers?!



238

00:17:22.792 --> 00:17:26.792

What are you after by calling us murderers?!



239

00:17:26.792 --> 00:17:28.250

Do you want us to regret it?



240

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:29.792

Do you want us to apologize?!



241

00:17:29.792 --> 00:17:31.708

Would that give you satisfaction?



242

00:17:31.708 --> 00:17:34.375

The people you thought we were no longer exist!



243

00:17:34.375 --> 00:17:39.125

If screaming will make you feel better,

then scream your damn head off!



244

00:17:52.375 --> 00:17:54.125

That's right...



245

00:17:55.417 --> 00:17:57.792

I'm still...



246

00:17:57.792 --> 00:17:59.667

...too naïve.



247

00:18:01.125 --> 00:18:03.000

I've...



248

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.458

...gotta do what I can.



249

00:18:05.458 --> 00:18:07.958

Do what I can...



250

00:18:07.958 --> 00:18:09.417

...to make you guys...



251

00:18:09.417 --> 00:18:12.875

...suffer and die in the worst way possible.



252

00:18:12.875 --> 00:18:14.875

You've got it coming.



253

00:18:22.708 --> 00:18:25.417

You can't be serious.



254

00:18:25.417 --> 00:18:26.875

Huh?



255

00:18:26.875 --> 00:18:28.667

Quit it, Eren.



256

00:18:28.667 --> 00:18:32.917

If you keep saying childish crap like that,

I've got no hope for you.



257

00:18:32.917 --> 00:18:34.333

Huh?!



258

00:18:37.792 --> 00:18:39.667

Hey, Reiner.



259

00:18:41.917 --> 00:18:44.125

What's the deal with that monkey?



260

00:18:47.417 --> 00:18:49.917

Monkey? What do you mean?



261

00:18:49.917 --> 00:18:53.083

Hmm? You don't know?



262

00:18:53.083 --> 00:19:00.250

That's surprising, given how much you two stared

at it with stars in your eyes like two little brats.



263

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:02.458

That monkey...



264

00:19:02.458 --> 00:19:05.625

What's that? A monkey?



265

00:19:05.625 --> 00:19:07.625

Just listen.



266

00:19:07.625 --> 00:19:13.000

That monkey Beast Titan

is what caused this recent fiasco.



267

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.625

It made Titans rise up from within the wall.



268

00:19:16.625 --> 00:19:20.917

I wonder if he was trying to assess our strength.



269

00:19:20.917 --> 00:19:24.375

That's where these guys are trying to get.



270

00:19:24.375 --> 00:19:30.167

If you guys get to him,

you'll be able to go back home, right?



271

00:19:30.167 --> 00:19:32.708

You... knew this?



272

00:19:32.708 --> 00:19:35.375

What do you know?! Tell me everything!



273

00:19:35.375 --> 00:19:38.625

Just wait. I've got circumstances of my own.



274

00:19:38.625 --> 00:19:41.667

What the hell do you mean by that?!



275

00:19:41.667 --> 00:19:45.833

Eren... if you think killing these two

will bring an end to everything...



276

00:19:45.833 --> 00:19:47.583

...you're gravely mistaken.



277

00:19:47.583 --> 00:19:48.833

Huh?!



278

00:19:48.833 --> 00:19:50.708

Then who's the enemy?!



279

00:19:50.708 --> 00:19:52.292

Enemy?



280

00:19:52.292 --> 00:19:53.583

If I said that, the--



281

00:19:53.583 --> 00:19:55.042

Ymir!



282

00:19:55.042 --> 00:19:59.208

Do you think there's any future for this world?



283

00:19:59.208 --> 00:20:03.000

If you know so much,

think about what you want to do.



284

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:07.125

It's not out of the question

for you to join our side.



285

00:20:07.125 --> 00:20:09.125

And trust you?



286

00:20:09.125 --> 00:20:12.833

Yeah, right. You two don't even trust me.



287

00:20:12.833 --> 00:20:15.625

Wrong. We can trust you.



288

00:20:15.625 --> 00:20:18.417

Because your one goal...



289

00:20:18.417 --> 00:20:20.833

...is to protect Christa.



290

00:20:22.875 --> 00:20:27.000

When it comes to her,

we should be able to trust one another.



291

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.833

You might think that I'm joking, but...



292

00:20:29.833 --> 00:20:36.042

Is it that hard for you to believe that

we might want the best for Christa as well?



293

00:20:36.042 --> 00:20:41.125

Or... would you rather put your hopes

in Eren and rely on him over us?



294

00:20:41.125 --> 00:20:42.708

Huh?!



295

00:20:45.667 --> 00:20:51.583

You're probably thinking your best chance

is to use Eren to escape from here.



296

00:20:51.583 --> 00:20:56.875

Because if you're taken by us,

there's little chance for your rescue.



297

00:20:56.875 --> 00:20:59.750

To be honest, that's pretty much true.



298

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:04.583

Even if you come with us,

we can't guarantee your safety.



299

00:21:04.583 --> 00:21:09.125

But if it's Christa we're talking about,

we might be able to do something for her.



300

00:21:11.917 --> 00:21:17.125

Will it be your petty life...

or Christa's future?



301

00:21:17.125 --> 00:21:19.333

It's up to you to decide.



302

00:21:20.333 --> 00:21:22.917

There's no future for this world?



303

00:21:22.917 --> 00:21:25.750

Why's that? What's this about a monkey?



304

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.458

What's going on?



305

00:21:28.458 --> 00:21:30.417

Hey!



306

00:21:30.417 --> 00:21:33.750

Hey, say something! Who's the enemy?!



307

00:21:35.083 --> 00:21:36.583

Ymir!



308

00:21:43.792 --> 00:21:46.083

Who knows...



309

00:21:46.083 --> 00:21:47.458

It's settled then.



310

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.542

Too bad, Eren.



311

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:04.000

The Scouts... are already...



312

00:22:05.875 --> 00:22:08.125

Dammit!



313

00:22:08.125 --> 00:22:09.500

Shit!



314

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:12.125

Damn you, Ymir.



315

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:18.208

There's just one hour left until sunset.



316

00:23:58.625 --> 00:24:01.208

As sunset swiftly approaches...



317

00:24:01.208 --> 00:24:07.417

...the Scout Regiment closes in, intent on

rescuing Eren from Reiner and Bertholdt.



318

00:24:07.417 --> 00:24:13.167

The pair plot to make their escape,

fleeing by use of ODM gear.



319

00:24:13.167 --> 00:24:21.208

However, reflecting on her past and emotions,

Ymir offers a plan of her own.



320

00:24:22.208 --> 00:24:27.072

Next episode: "Children."

